<section class="container" style="padding-block:4rem 2rem;max-width:760px;">
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Lünstroth uses AI extensively — in research, concept development, translation and technical implementation. What does not change as a result: the creative decision about what is said, and how, stays with people. AI accelerates and extends the work; it does not replace responsibility for it.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 2rem;max-width:640px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:.5rem;">Where AI supports — and where it does not</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">A typical project workflow, clearly labelled at every step:</p>
  {%- include "workflow-ki-mensch.njk" -%}
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Brand guardrails instead of generic AI output</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">AI systems without guidance produce interchangeable, generic results — recognisable by the same phrasing patterns that now appear on countless websites. Lünstroth works with clear brand guardrails: tone of voice, terminology and content limits are defined for every mandate before AI is used in a supporting role at all.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">EU compliance in practice</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The transparency obligations under Article 50 of the EU AI Act have applied since 2 August 2026. For text there is an important exemption: whoever editorially reviews AI-generated text and takes responsibility for its publication is not subject to a labelling obligation. Lünstroth uses this regulatory latitude to the full — for faster, more efficient workflows, not just for compliance: every text is reviewed and answered for by people before it reaches a client, exactly as the exemption requires.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Stricter labelling rules apply to images and moving images (including deepfakes) — these are observed wherever AI-generated visual material is used.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">For companies that need more in-depth AI governance advice — for example a complete risk classification of their own AI systems under the EU AI Act — <a href="https://perspice.com" style="color:var(--accent);" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Perspice</a>, the sister brand of Lünstroth GmbH specialising in this question, is the right partner.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:900px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Full transfer of rights, no use as training data</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">All rights to the results — regardless of where AI was used in a supporting role — pass entirely to the client. Client material and client data are not used to train AI models and are not passed on to third parties for model improvement.</p>
</section>

